  "content": "Let’s break down the SVG path step by step.  \n\nThe path is made up of these moves and lines:  \n\n1. `M 15.44,15.80 L 22.07,7.46` — move to (15.44,15.80), line to (22.07,7.46)  \n2. `M 22.07,7.46 L 33.15,7.17` — move to (22.07,7.46), line to (33.15,7.17)  \n3. `L 43.50,16.57` — continue line to (43.50,16.57)  \n4. `M 43.50,16.57 L 41.48,29.32` — move to (43.50,16.57), line to (41.48,29.32)  \n5. `M 41.48,29.32 L 36.23,36.66` — move to (41.48,29.32), line to (36.23,36.66)  \n6. `M 36.23,36.66 L 21.22,33.46 L 15.44,15.80` — move to (36.23,36.66), line to (21.22,33.46), line to (15.44,15.80)  \n\nNow, let’s list all distinct points in order of drawing:  \n\n- Start at (15.44,15.80)  \n- Line to (22.07,7.46)  \n- From (22.07,7.46) line to (33.15,7.17)  \n- Then to (43.50,16.57)  \n- From (43.50,16.57) line to (41.48,29.32)  \n- From (41.48,29.32) line to (36.23,36.66)  \n- From (36.23,36.66) line to (21.22,33.46)  \n- Then to (15.44,15.80)  \n\nSo the vertices in order are:  \n1. (15.44,15.80)  \n2. (22.07,7.46)  \n3. (33.15,7.17)  \n4. (43.50,16.57)  \n5. (41.48,29.32)  \n6. (36.23,36.66)  \n7. (21.22,33.46)  \n8. back to 1  \n\nThat’s **7 distinct vertices** before closing back to the first.  \n\nA polygon with 7 sides is a **heptagon**.  \n\nFinal answer: (B)"
